sequenceDiagram
  %% Container runtime (docs/reference/development-containers.md#a-stopped-nested-fleet-clone-starts): `instance:wake` of a clone of a nested-fleet default starts the stopped copy and its inner fleet. A nested-fleet clone never sleeps, so this is its only Orbit start after its create.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: instance:wake
  %% kind: instance.start
  autonumber
  %% lane CL icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CL as Caller<br/>orbit · task flow
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant N as app-dev Node<br/>Instance container
  CL->>GW: instance:wake INSTANCE
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit instance:wake INSTANCE`
  %%> Callers:
  %%> - the command, after a host reboot, an OOM kill or a stop by hand left the copy stopped
  %%> - never a Route visit: the runtime activation endpoint admits only a wake, and a nested-fleet clone has no asleep marker
  %%> - planned: the task flow before it uses a task's copy
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the caller is the Instance's Node or has node access to it
  Note over GW: Start or join the start<br/>one per Instance
  %%> When:
  %%> - an active development clone of a nested-fleet default, on a Node with the nested-fleet switch on
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the wake admits `instance.start` instead of `instance.wake`; an Idempotency-Key keys the start
  %%> - an open start of the Instance is joined; any other Operation on the Instance refuses it with `operation.target_busy`
  %%> On failure:
  %%> - a nested-fleet default: `instance.sleep_unsupported`; it starts only through its deployment
  %%> - other lifecycle work: `instance.lifecycle_busy`; no run starts
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-instance-start
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the run's one read of the Club key; without one the start fails before its run with `instance.nested_club_key_missing`
  GW-->>CL: 202 Accepted<br/>Operation ID
  SW->>N: Start the container<br/>Ansible · tags start
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the start guard: `boot.autostart=false`, the egress gates of every bridge NIC
  %%> - `incus start`, then the Club key into the container's /run (tmpfs) on stdin, the same script as the create's `clone-club-key`
  %%> - waits until each desired-running unit is active; T3 starts with the container, and the start does not wait for it
  %%> Why:
  %%> - no seed or snapshot holds the key, so every start delivers it before the fleet checks
  SW->>N: Start the inner fleet<br/>Ansible · fleet check, resume
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the create's `clone-fleet`: the fleet rules, the three nested containers, the tunnel `wg-nested`
  %%> - waits for Doctor over the tunnel and the three agents
  %%> - records its own seconds as `fleet_seconds`
  alt the run passes
    %% path: main
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal result
    Note over GW: Record running
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the runtime's `power_state` is `running`
    %%> - `nested_fleet_club_key` says what the start did with the key; `fleet_seconds` the fleet's time
  else a step fails
    %% path: failed
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed step, error_code
    %%> Result:
    %%> - a fleet failure names why in the failure's detail, redacted
    %%> - the container may run with a fleet that is not ready; `power_state` stays as it was
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - the same command; each step leaves what already runs as it is
  end
  loop until terminal
    CL->>GW: operation:show TASK
    GW-->>CL: Status and result
  end
